cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tldr: a compression contract for AI coding agents"
message: "If you use or reference this project, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Surefire Studios"
    website: "https://github.com/SurefireStudios"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SurefireStudios/tldr"
url: "https://github.com/SurefireStudios/tldr"
abstract: >-
  A skill for AI coding agents that leads every response with a three-line
  TL;DR and keeps the full detail directly underneath, rather than deleting it.
  Includes a parseable block format for agent-to-agent reports, and an
  evaluation harness that measures output-token reduction alongside a fidelity
  score, so compression cannot be claimed as a win when it loses information.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - ai agents
  - summarization
  - context engineering
  - token optimization
  - human computer interaction
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-11"
